{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1000", "sample_idx": 13, "model_name": "meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct", "content": "Raymond III Count of Tripoli was a ruler of the County of Tripoli a Crusader state established in the Levant region after the First Crusade. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. \n\nRaymond III is first mentioned in 1152 as the Count of Tripoli. He ruled the county until his death in 1187. The County of Tripoli was an important state in the region and played a key role in the Crusader's struggle against the Muslim forces. \n\n* **Early Life and Reign** *\n\nRaymond III was a member of the House of Tripoli a noble family that originated from the region of Occitania in southern France. He was the son of Raymond II Count of Tripoli and Hodierna of Jerusalem. Raymond II had married Hodierna in 1133 and they had two children together Raymond III and Alice. \n\nRaymond III was a skilled military leader and played a key role in the Crusader's struggle against the Muslim forces. He was also a diplomat and formed alliances with other Crusader states in the region. \n\n**Military Campaigns** *\n\nRaymond III participated in several military campaigns during his reign. In 1160 he led a military campaign against the Muslim forces in the region of Galilee. The Crusaders were successful in their campaign and they were able to capture several key cities in the region. \n\nIn 1164 Raymond III participated in the Battle of Harenc a major battle between the Crusaders and the Muslim forces. The Crusaders were defeated in the battle and many of their leaders were killed. Raymond III was able to escape the battle and he returned to Tripoli. \n\n**Death and Succession** *\n\nRaymond III died in 1187 during the reign of Saladin a Muslim leader who had conquered much of the Middle East. The County of Tripoli was a key target for Saladin and he launched a series of attacks against the county in 1187. Raymond III was killed in one of these battles and the county was conquered by the Muslim forces. \n\nThe County of Tripoli was conquered by the Muslim forces in 1187 and it became a province of the Ayyubid Empire. The county was eventually reconquered by the Crusaders in 1191 but it was never able to recover its former power and influence.", "logprobs": [{"token": "Ray", "logprob": -0.014390614}, {"token": "mond", "logprob": -0.00016938205}, {"token": " III", "logprob": -0.0010648064}, {"token": " Count", "logprob": -0.1300828}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -3.349725e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.00021371941}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -6.651657e-05}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.015882885}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.34376433}, {"token": " ruler", "logprob": -2.3370414}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.08210078}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.022185005}, {"token": " County", "logprob": -0.43109655}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -1.1086402e-05}, {"token": " Trip", "logprob": -0.0002349339}, {"token": "oli", "logprob": -7.3072624e-05}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -1.1298783}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.4285146}, {"token": "ader", "logprob": -0.00019178935}, {"token": " state", "logprob": -0.0121175805}, {"token": " established", "logprob": -1.5330064}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.3475098}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.43807077}, {"token": " Lev", "logprob": -0.081108235}, {"token": "ant", "logprob": -0.00052009406}, {"token": " region", "logprob": -2.525834}, {"token": " after", "logprob": -2.279444}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.002599553}, {"token": " First", "logprob": -0.03947167}, {"token": " Crus", "logprob": -0.00042489084}, {"token": "ade", "logprob": -1.0490363e-05}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.08828332}, {"token": " He", "logprob": -0.24499418}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -0.14687832}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -0.45791072}, {"token": " son", "logprob": -0.17107095}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.0041700555}, {"token": " Raymond", "logprob": -0.57563674}, {"t